RESEARCH REFLECTION for masked_contact_coupling_net_loop2c_001:
Conclusion  : Good / provisional new best: lr_auprc=0.528 is the first scored run, so there is no baseline or prior best to compare against. It is well above the hypothesised 0.25-0.30 and the ~0.11 random level. Secondary metrics agree: lr_auroc 0.847 and direction_accuracy 0.775. The run is non-degenerate. Health gates passed, with 10 distinct symbols and a dominant-symbol fraction of 0.10, so there was no collapse. It was a formal run at full portion (1.0), so data volume is not a concern.
Key Factor  : A very small masked contact-coupling network (1495 params) trained with smooth_l1 loss for 40 epochs at full formal data scope. Loss_type and architecture size are the main levers, but no other runs exist to isolate either.
Discovery   : A tiny 1.5k-parameter model gives strong ranking performance (AUPRC about 5x the random level). Training dynamics are healthy. Train loss fell from 0.02468 to 0.02220, and validation fell from 0.02410 to 0.02328. The gap is small (+0.0011) and stable, so there is no overfitting. Validation is noisy epoch to epoch (best at epoch 37 of 40, final +0.00033 above best), and it fluctuates by about ±0.0005. Train loss plateaued after about epoch 15 (about 0.0220-0.0222), which suggests the model is capacity- or signal-limited rather than undertrained. Validation smooth_l1 differences of this size are not reliable guides to model selection. Use lr_auprc instead.
Memory Update: Treat this run as the reference point: smooth_l1, 1495 params, 40 epochs, lr_auprc 0.528 (auroc 0.847, dir_acc 0.775). Smooth_l1 final_loss of 0.0222 is the same-loss reference for future runs. No baseline score exists, so record this as the baseline. The next step should be to test capacity: increase hidden width or latent dims modestly, since the loss plateau and small train/val gap indicate headroom. Keep loss_type and the data scope fixed so the effect can be attributed. Do not extend epochs, because the loss was flat after about epoch 15. Shorter training (about 20-25 epochs) may give a high-efficiency candidate at the same score. Repeat with another seed to measure score variance before treating differences under about 5% as real. Do not recommend a change to trial_portion, because formal scope is operator-set.
